{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.genus_handle_available_at_no_component_of_the_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.genus_handle_available_at_no_component_of_the_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.lean#L148-L152","doc":"**Applied to the carrier**: for `A ≥ 1` the closure has `μ = A + 1 ≥ 2`\ncomponents and the handle is available at none of them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.atomCarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.atomCarrier","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.lean#L133-L146","doc":"The derived carrier's measured linking data: components `Fin m`, consecutive\npairs carrying `-2`, everything else `0`.\n\nInstantiated so the theorem above is demonstrably about a real configuration rather\nthan an empty hypothesis. The value `-2` is what the probe measures in the\nall-`σ⁻¹` branch; nothing below depends on it beyond being nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.no_component_is_brunnian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.no_component_is_brunnian","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.lean#L103-L131","doc":"**The result.** On a path of at least two components, *no* component has all\nits linking numbers vanishing — so the Borromean hypothesis of the complement-genus\nestimate fails at every single one.\n\nThe endpoint is the case worth stating: the last component has no successor, and the\nargument closes it by walking backwards through `lk_symm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.PathLinking.consecutive_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.PathLinking.consecutive_ne","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.lean#L101-L101","doc":"consecutive components are genuinely linked ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.PathLinking.lk_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.PathLinking.lk_symm","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.lean#L99-L99","doc":"linking is symmetric in its two components ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.PathLinking.lk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.PathLinking.lk","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.lean#L97-L97","doc":"the pairwise linking numbers ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.PathLinking.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.PathLinking.mk","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.PathLinking","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.PathLinking","kind":"structure","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.lean#L88-L101","doc":"**The measured shape of the derived carrier**: `m` components whose linking\ngraph is the path `P_m` — consecutive components linked, and (as recorded in\n`lk_symm`) linking is symmetric.\n\nOnly the two facts the theorem uses are demanded. In particular nothing here says\nthe *non*-consecutive pairs vanish; the conclusion does not need it, and demanding\nit would make the structure harder to instantiate than the result requires. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.brunnianAt_of_all_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.brunnianAt_of_all_zero","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.lean#L81-L86","doc":"**The predicate is inhabited** — on an unlinked (or genuinely Brunnian)\nconfiguration every component satisfies it. Recorded so `no_component_is_brunnian`\nbelow cannot be read as vacuous: it is a statement about *this* carrier's shape, not\na statement that `BrunnianAt` is unsatisfiable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.not_brunnianAt_of_linked","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.not_brunnianAt_of_linked","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.lean#L77-L79","doc":"One linked partner is enough to destroy the hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.BrunnianAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.BrunnianAt","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeGenusHandleNeedsVanishingLinking.lean#L65-L75","doc":"**The hypothesis the genus handle needs at component `k`**: every pairwise\nlinking number of `k` with the other components vanishes.\n\nThis is the Brunnian condition localised at one component, and it is exactly what\nmakes a surface bounded by `L_k` in the complement of the rest exist at all.\n\n**TIER 3.**  It is the pointwise form of `MilnorIndeterminacyGate`'s tier-2\ncondition — `BrunnianTierDisambiguation.linkingVanishes_iff_forall_at` proves the\ntwo agree on a symmetric three-component matrix — and, like it, is strictly\nweaker than true Brunnian-ness.  Tier table for the four things this corpus calls `Brunnian`, and which implications hold: `QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}